// The boss journal: Vhalgrath, the Ember Wyrm, in each hero's own words (docs/plans/journal-voices.md)
(window.JOURNAL_DATA = window.JOURNAL_DATA || {}).wyrm = {
  // the first time this hero meets him (after the first pull)
  meet: {
    bastion: "The dragon walks after whoever holds him, then leaves the ground altogether and comes back down where he likes. A line cannot hold what is not there. Learned to watch the sky. Gave ground.",
    gloomsworn: "The Wyrm follows whoever stands before him, then leaves the earth and comes down wherever he pleases. I cannot guard what is not there. I looked up. I have lain under worse skies, and I was dead for those.",
    thresher: "Vhalgrath is weather with wings: drought on the ground, then hail out of a clear sky wherever he likes. I learned to watch where the embers drew his road down before he came. Nothing ripens on a hill that hot. Not yet.",
    bloodreaver: "Finally, one with real fire in him! Claws like plough blades, a breath that cooks the floor, and then he flew off before I'd finished enjoying it. Cheeky. I want him back on the ground.",
    runeguard: "The Wyrm keeps two courts, one on the ground and one in the air, and the omens differ between them. The air gives warning; the ground gives none that I have read yet. Not foreseen; now it will be.",
    gorgemaw: "A roast of the first rank: a great black beast, fire in the belly, served from the sky. I am told it is too hot to eat. I will be the judge of that. I came away hungry.",
    oathbroker: "The Tyrant holds the crater by right of age, and enforces it by fire. Every term is read out in the air before it lands, but one must be there to read it. I was not. Breach noted.",
    ironpalm: "He came down from the sky and spoke with fire. I answered too slowly. The ground here is warm and uneven. Breathe. Listen to the wings.",
    ranger: "Big. Black. Flies when it chooses and lands where it likes. No line on a thing that will not stay on the ground. Watched where it came from, not where it went.",
    shadowblade: "The mark has the whole sky to hide in, which is cheating. When it comes down it comes down loudly. Waited at its flank and counted its blind side. Will try again.",
    pyromancer: "A DRAGON! Fire, and he is better at it than I am! I have never been so insulted, or so delighted. The floor was glowing the colour of trouble all night. Hair intact, barely.",
    thermist: "Hot. All of him, and the ground he spat on. I ran hot with admiration and then burnt my boots. The sky was cold; that part I liked. Back to the middle, next time.",
    driftblade: "He took off and I wanted to follow him, which is not allowed, and then he came down like a falling mountain on the far side of the crater, and I ran through the ash for the whole of it.",
    marionettist: "Our leading man arrives by air, which is vulgar and effective. Three scorched marks in the floor, and he picks one for his entrance. The company was not cued. (My Doll was singed, and sulked.)",
    cleric: "An old tyrant on a hot hill, and nobody he did not burn a little. He is not cruel; he is simply very large. I had more to mend than I could reach. Dawn keep us. Back to it.",
    grovekeeper: "A drought and a fire in one animal. The ground does not take the seed where he has breathed. Everything he does comes from above, like weather, and I am not used to weather that chooses.",
    chronomancer: "He rises, he falls, he lands, and each time he lands I will have been standing in the wrong place. The warning is long, the beat is exact, and this time I found it. Not first time.",
    alembist: "Specimen: one dragon, very old, very warm. Ailments: burns, shocks, and a floor that bites for some time after. The shelves ran low by the first descent. One flask went off. Not mine.",
    threadweaver: "He hovers over the whole crater like a loose thread and drops where he pleases. My stitches kept running into the last place he'd been. A sloppy seam, entirely mine.",
  },
  // the first time this hero beats him
  win: {
    bastion: "The Wyrm is down. The line held the ground through the flights and the burning rim, and the crater is quiet. A long way past the Barrow, and still standing. Held.",
    gloomsworn: "He is down. The crater is quiet, and I am still here, which still surprises me. A long post. Someone else may keep the watch a while.",
    thresher: "Vhalgrath has come in at last, and the crater can lie fallow a while. I said a few kind words over him; he was old weather, and old weather earns them. Something new in me, not yet ripe.",
    bloodreaver: "The big one is down, and every scar he gave me is still warm. The best fire I have ever taken, and I took all of it. I will remember his heart opening for the rest of my life.",
    runeguard: "The Wyrm is judged, and the air with him. I read the sky at last: every line drawn before it was walked, every fire shown before it fell. As foreseen, finally.",
    gorgemaw: "The roast is carved. Smoke, ash and a touch of old bone. I ate until I could not feel my teeth, and it was well worth the burn. Slightly overdone. Magnificent.",
    oathbroker: "The Tyrant's claim on the crater is voided, and the account is closed. We paid in full, and the final instalment came due in the heart of him. Countersigned.",
    ironpalm: "He spoke his last word with fire, and we answered it from the ground. The crater is quiet now. Breathe.",
    ranger: "The old dragon is down. The wind in the crater is mine now. Clean line, at last.",
    shadowblade: "The mark came down and stayed down. For once, the sky was empty and so was he. It never saw me, and in the end it never saw anything.",
    pyromancer: "I outshone a DRAGON! Briefly, and only in the last moment, but it counts. My robes are a disgrace. My heart is not. Mostly unsinged, if you do not look at the sleeves.",
    thermist: "He fell, and the whole crater went still. Hot to the end, then cold, and a quiet in the middle where I like to stand. Back to the middle. At last.",
    driftblade: "He fell out of the sky for the last time, and I ran out through the smoke and up the ribs of older kills and never once landed, and the wind went with me.",
    marionettist: "Final curtain for the star of the air. The company stood to the very end, and the Doll took the last bow. (Applause. The crater echoed it.)",
    cleric: "The old tyrant is at rest, and the crater is cooling. We walked down from the peaks, all of us. Thank the light, and thank every one of us who stood in it.",
    grovekeeper: "The fire is out of him. The crater will take seed again, in time. Plant first, and leave the ashes alone for a season. My lot came through all of it.",
    chronomancer: "He fell, and I did not have to undo a thing. That is the first time with a dragon. I will have been proud of us, I suppose. I am now.",
    alembist: "Result: one dragon, extinguished. Shelves nearly bare, every patient alive. A new reagent has appeared in the heart of the crater, not mine. Labelled: do not touch.",
    threadweaver: "He is unpicked at last, and the whole hem came home. There is a seam in the sky where he used to hang, and I did not tie it. Pulled it tight regardless.",
  },
  moves: {
    "Tyrant's Roar": { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "He roared and it reached every one of us. Nothing to block, nowhere to stand that was not in it. I kept the line close to our healer, footing set, and took it standing. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "His roar went through every one of us, and no shield was any use against sound. I stood close to the one who mends and let the dark take its share of me. It was a long note.",
      thresher: "His roar comes down on all of us at once, and there's no hedge to stand behind. I topped myself up before his throat swelled and kept my hands busy through it. Lovely lungs, though.",
      bloodreaver: "The roar went through my ribs and every one of my friends' too. Barely a scratch for me, shameful, but they felt it, so I stayed near the one who mends and let them be topped up after.",
      runeguard: "The omen: his throat swells and the air shakes. The answer: it reaches the whole crater and no ward turns it, so each of us must be whole before it sounds. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "The roar is a course served to the whole table at once, and I cannot eat it for anyone. So we sat close, came to it well fed, and swallowed it together. Smoky.",
      oathbroker: "The Roar is a levy on every one of the undersigned, payable at once; no clause excuses anyone. The fine print: arrive at it already mended. We did. Entered in the ledger.",
      ironpalm: "He spoke to all of us at once, loudly. There is no answering it. We came to it whole and let it pass through us. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Roar. Reaches everyone, no cover from it. Mended before, kept drawing through it. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "The mark roared and it found everyone, even me, which was rude. Nothing to hide behind, so I made sure I was whole when it sounded and went back to work.",
      pyromancer: "The roar made my hair stand on end, and he does it better than me! There is no escaping it, so I made sure I was not half-scorched when it came, and kept casting through it. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "The roar goes through everyone. Cold fact. Be whole before it. Then it hit and I ran hot with it, rattled, still swinging. Back to the middle.",
      driftblade: "He roared across the whole crater and there was no running through it or round it, nowhere to go, which offends me, so I came to it whole and kept moving through the sound.",
      marionettist: "The star opened his mouth and the whole house shook, stalls and wings alike. No exits; the company came to it whole and played on. (The Doll did not flinch.)",
      cleric: "The roar fell on every one of us. I mended everyone before it came, not after, and laid a little grace over the faithful as he lifted his head. Dawn keep us.",
      grovekeeper: "The roar comes like hail: no cover, my lot all at once. Plant first. I had the mending growing in everyone before it broke.",
      chronomancer: "The roar lands a beat after his throat swells. I had everyone mended in the moment before; next time, which was last time, I will start a beat earlier.",
      alembist: "Ailment: the roar, felt by everyone, no hiding from it. Remedy: the whole party whole before it sounds, the big brew poured over everyone just ahead. Front shelf.",
      threadweaver: "The roar ran along every thread at once. No tying it off. We stood close, I pulled the slack tight, and we took it in common. Mind the slack.",
    } },
    'Rending Claws': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The claws came down on me alone, a wide rake in front of him. I waited for the shoulder to drop, shield up in the last instant, and kept the others out of the arc. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "The claws were meant for me. I watched his near shoulder and let the rake land where I stood. A wound is only a wound; mine are written down already. The rest kept wide of the arc.",
      thresher: "The claws come in on our knight, a wide rake across the front of him, like a harrow dragged the wrong way. I stayed at his flank, well out of the arc, and kept working his side. Not my row, that one.",
      bloodreaver: "The claws! A deep one across the front of him, and the wound stays good and open. Barely a scratch, shameful. I braced, took it, and answered it while it was fresh.",
      runeguard: "The omen: he rears and the near claw lifts. The answer: a ward a breath before, the others well outside the arc in front of him. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "The claws are served to me alone, a heavy rake with a sauce that runs. I opened wide just before it, kept my friends off my plate, and chewed. Rare, and good.",
      oathbroker: "The Claws are payable by whoever stands before him, and the fine print is how wide the arc runs. I accepted delivery behind every protection I had, the undersigned kept clear. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "He raked once, wide. I did not raise my arms until its last instant, and took half. Then I answered. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Claws. Wide arc in front of it. Kept to its flank, outside the rake, and drew again before the dust settled. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "The mark raked at whoever faced it, which was not me. I kept to its side, where neither claw could find me, and came back in when it was done. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "He raked the ground in front of him and I decided I did not need to be there! I stood off to the side and finished my spell from the edge. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Claws: cold, wide, in front. Step to the side. Then the heat came and I swung back in at once, cutting, behind the swing and not in it. Back to the middle.",
      driftblade: "The rake came round in front of him and I went through his side and out the back of it and round again, never landing, and it was over before I had even slowed.",
      marionettist: "Our leading man swept the stage in front of him. The company stepped to the wings on cue and my Doll slipped out behind. (Applause for the Doll, mostly.)",
      cleric: "The claws fell on our knight, as they always do. I laid the light on him before they landed instead of after, and he barely staggered. Dawn keep him.",
      grovekeeper: "The big rake came on like a squall, front of him only. I had planted on our knight before it, so the mending was already growing when it struck. Plant first.",
      chronomancer: "The claws land a beat after the shoulder drops. I had the warding on our knight in the moment before; I will have been early. I was.",
      alembist: "Ailment: the claws, one heavy rake, front of him only. Remedy: a ward on whoever stands there, and everyone else kept out of the arc. Label it plainly.",
      threadweaver: "The rake landed on our knight, and it ran down my thread to the archer, so neither took all of it. A neat seam. Mind the slack, and mind the front of him.",
    } },
    'Ember Breath': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "He breathed at one of us, not me, and the fan of fire followed them. I kept the line clear of the long flames and out of the glowing ground it left behind. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "The breath chose someone else, and followed them. I kept clear of its length and off the scorched floor after, which lingers. I know something of lingering.",
      thresher: "The breath picks one of us and follows them like a sheepdog till the last. Whoever it is waits, then steps aside late, not back. The ground it scorches stays bad a good while; I kept off it like a burnt field.",
      bloodreaver: "A cone of fire! And it follows whoever he picks until the last moment. I like that. Step aside late and sideways, and keep off the molten ground after. A fine scar, not mine.",
      runeguard: "The omen: his head goes back and the fire gathers; it tracks its quarry until the last. The answer: leave the fan sideways, late, and stay off the molten ground it leaves. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "The breath is a flambe, served at one guest and following them round the table. Step out of the line at the last, and do not stand on the plate afterwards. Overcooked.",
      oathbroker: "The Breath is served on one named party, and the fine print is that it follows them, and then lingers on the floor. Clear the line, then clear the ground. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "He spoke fire at one of us. It followed. I did not run, I stepped aside, late. Then I stayed off the hot ground. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Breath at one of us. Tracks till late. Stepped out sideways at the last, not back. The floor burns for a while after. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "The mark breathed at someone else, which was lovely of it. The fire follows them until the last moment, so they step aside late. The ground burns afterwards. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "He breathed fire at one of us and I felt I should have been consulted! It follows them until the last instant; step off sideways and keep clear of the glowing floor. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Breath: hot, narrow, tracking. Step aside, late. Cold read after: the ground stays molten, stay off it. I was not cold enough. Too far, the other way. Back to the middle.",
      driftblade: "The fire came after one of us in a long sweep and I ran through its edge and out the side just as it set, and the floor behind it was glowing and I went round that too, never landing.",
      marionettist: "The star breathed at one member of the company, and the beam followed them across the stage. Sidestep at the last cue; the boards afterward burn for a time. (The Doll walked round them.)",
      cleric: "The fire hunted one of my flock and followed her across the floor. I told her: wait, and step aside late, and mind the floor after. Dawn keep her. She did.",
      grovekeeper: "The breath comes like a grass fire, in a line after one of my lot. Wait, step aside, and keep off the scorched ground; nothing grows there for a time. Plant after.",
      chronomancer: "The fire tracks its quarry until a beat before it lands. I stepped aside on that beat and not before. The ground burned for a time after. Next time, which was last time, I stood further off.",
      alembist: "Ailment: a cone of fire at one of us, tracking, and a floor that burns afterwards. Remedy: step aside late, then keep off the glow. Label the floor too.",
      threadweaver: "The fire chased one stitch across the floor. Wait for the last moment, step out sideways, and keep every thread off the glowing ground. A burnt hem is a sloppy hem.",
    } },
    'Tail Lash': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "He swept the tail round behind him, not in front. I held my footing at his front and the line stood to his sides. Whoever stood at his back learned it. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "The tail swung behind him. I stood before his face, the rest at his flanks. Whoever stood at his back learned it the way I learned dying: once.",
      thresher: "The tail comes round behind him like a flail on the threshing floor. I work from his side, never his back, and it passes me by. Whoever stood behind him learned it in one season.",
      bloodreaver: "The tail! Behind him, a wide sweep, and I was in front for once. A good one, but not mine. The ones behind him were not so pleased. Stay at his sides.",
      runeguard: "The omen: his shoulders turn and the tail rises. The answer: the sweep is behind him, so the line stands at his sides or his front, and no one behind. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "The tail is a side dish, served at the back of the table. Whoever sat at the back got the lot. I sat at the head, as a gourmand should. Underseasoned.",
      oathbroker: "The fine print of the Tail is its location: behind him, never in front. Those who stood behind were in breach. The undersigned stood to the sides. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "He swung the tail behind him. I stood in front and did not move. Those behind moved. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Tail. Behind it, wide arc. Kept to its flank and shot over the shoulder. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "The mark swung its tail behind it, which is where I usually stand. Rude. Moved to its side, where neither end can see me. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "He swung that tail behind him and I was standing in just the wrong place, glowing! Learned to stand at his side. Mostly unsinged, and a little bruised.",
      thermist: "Tail: behind him. Step to the side. Then the heat came and I was swinging back in, from the flank, not the rear. Back to the middle.",
      driftblade: "The tail came round behind him in a great arc and I went through the gap beside it, out the front and round again, never landing, and never behind him.",
      marionettist: "The star's tail swept the upstage. I had my Doll in the wings and the company at his sides, where the arc does not reach. (A respectable review.)",
      cleric: "The tail swept behind him and caught a friend who had wandered there. Dawn keep her. I told her to keep to his sides, and mended what I could.",
      grovekeeper: "The tail comes round like a storm cloud behind him. Keep to his flanks and the weather passes you by. My lot learned it the first time. Plant first.",
      chronomancer: "The tail lands a beat after he turns his shoulder, behind him. I stood at his side on that beat. I will have known it, I think. This time, I did.",
      alembist: "Ailment: the tail, a wide sweep behind him. Remedy: stand at his flanks or his front and nowhere in the arc. Note: the shelf behind him is not safe, either.",
      threadweaver: "The tail swept his back, and anyone stitched in there came away torn. Mind the slack, and mind the seam. My stitches stand at his flanks now.",
    } },
    'Magma Burst': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The marks came up over the others, not me. I held his front while each took their own patch of floor, and they stepped off their own pools when it struck. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "Marks rose over every head but mine. Each of them took a place apart and left the pool when it burst, and no one needed me for it. A rare quiet job.",
      thresher: "A ring came up over each of us but our knight, and every one wanted its own plot. I walked out to mine, apart from the others, let it come in, then stepped off the pool it left. Soft ground, that.",
      bloodreaver: "Little circles of fire over my friends, and each leaves a puddle of molten rock. I stayed with the big one and let them handle theirs. Step out of your puddle, fast.",
      runeguard: "The omen: marks over each of us, save the one in front. The answer: each takes a patch of their own, apart, then leaves the pool they leave behind. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "The marks were little canapés over my friends' heads, each landing in a puddle of sauce. I did not eat one. Each took their own plate and left it afterwards. Hot, hot, hot.",
      oathbroker: "The fine print of the Burst: each marked party owes a circle of their own, and the pool remains after. Do not share, and do not stand in your debt. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "The marks came over the others. They parted. Each stood alone, and each stepped out of what they left. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Marks over the others. Fanned out, one patch each. Stepped out of the pools after. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "The marks went over everyone but me, and I spent the moment thinking how nice that was. Each of them took their own patch, then left the pool behind. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "Marks over my head, which I took as a compliment! Each of us needed our own patch of floor, and each leaves a pool of molten rock. Stepped out of mine quickly. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Marks. Apart, each alone. Then the pool underfoot: out of it at once. I was in mine too long, ran hot, and had to be mended. Back to the middle, not the pool.",
      driftblade: "The marks came and I ran to my own patch at the far edge, and the others fanned out, and when it struck I was already running, out of the pool and through the gap and round again.",
      marionettist: "Each of us got our own spotlight, and each spotlight leaves a hot patch on the boards. The company fanned out wide, and left their marks at once. (My Doll was spared the lights.)",
      cleric: "The marks fell on my flock, each on their own. I told them: apart, and out of the pool you leave behind. Dawn keep them. I mended the one who forgot.",
      grovekeeper: "The marks came like scattered seed, one over each of my lot. Everyone took their own ground, and when it fell they stepped out of the molten patch. Plant first.",
      chronomancer: "The marks land a beat after they appear, and the pool arrives with them. I will have stepped off my own after the first beat. I did.",
      alembist: "Ailment: marks over each of us, then a puddle of molten rock. Remedy: apart from each other for the mark, then off the puddle at once. Keep the flasks well apart, too.",
      threadweaver: "Each mark wanted its own seam, so I cut the threads before they snapped and tied them again after we regrouped. And off the molten patch. Mind the slack.",
    } },
    'Cinder Feast': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "He marked one of us for a hit that had to be shared. I closed the line on them and took my share, standing in the ring, and we split it. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "One of us wore a ring to be shared. I walked in beside them, the rest followed, and the weight was cut into pieces small enough to carry. Nothing is heavy that many hands bear.",
      thresher: "A blue ring over one of us, and it's a load to share, like a cart nobody pulls alone. All of us in under it together, and it came in light. Leave a hand out and the rest carry more.",
      bloodreaver: "A blow too big for one! We all piled in on the marked one and split it between us. A fine scar each. Stand close, stand in the ring, and bleed together.",
      runeguard: "The omen: a ring over one of us, blue at the edge. The answer: it is a share, so everyone stands in it together, and it is divided among us. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "A dish for the whole table, to be shared, the ring marked on the floor. We all sat down in it together and took a portion each. Large, and filling.",
      oathbroker: "The Feast is a debt owed in common: the undersigned stand in the ring together, and it is divided among them. The fine print is that nobody absents themselves. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "A blow for one, spoken to all. We stood in the ring together and listened together. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Ring over one of us, blue. Share it: all of us in the ring at once. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "The mark chose one of us and I stood in the ring with the others, which I hate. It was shared among us, and thin by the time it reached me. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "A hit too big to take alone! We all stood in the ring together, which I resented, then I admitted it was right. It was shared between us. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "The ring on one of us. Hot, big, shared. Everyone in, together, close. I ran hot with fright and stayed in. Back to the middle.",
      driftblade: "The hit we had to share meant standing still with everyone, which I hate, so I ran a circle round the ring until the very last breath and then slipped in among them and took it.",
      marionettist: "The star pointed at one of the company and demanded a shared bow. The whole company crowded into the ring and took it as one. A tolerable second act.",
      cleric: "He marked one of my flock for a great hit, and we all gathered round her in the ring, so it was divided. Dawn keep her. I stood in it with them.",
      grovekeeper: "A great blow came to one, and we all gathered under it like trees in a storm and split the weight. Everyone in the ring. Plant first, and stand close.",
      chronomancer: "The ring lands a beat after it blooms. I was inside it a beat before, with the others, and it was divided. Nearly nobody was undone.",
      alembist: "Ailment: one of us marked for a blow too large to bear alone. Remedy: everyone in the ring at once, to divide the dose. Mind the pool, too.",
      threadweaver: "The ring wanted all of us together, so I tied the threads in close and we stood in it as one. Divided among us, it was nothing. Mind the slack.",
    } },
    'Dragonfall': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "He rose, and embers drew a line across the floor, out of the sky to a scorched pit. The line and the circle at its end were what hurt. Held the ground, stayed clear of both. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "He rose out of sight, and the embers drew his road to a pit. The road hurts, and so does the ring at its end. I stood clear of both and watched him arrive on nothing.",
      thresher: "Up he went, and the embers drew his road to one of the pits, the ring showing which. I stepped off the road and well clear of the pit, and let him dig it himself. Saves me the trouble.",
      bloodreaver: "He dives! A line of embers from the edge, and a great red circle where he lands. I wanted to meet him there. I stayed off the line and out of the circle, for once, and bled elsewhere.",
      runeguard: "The omen: embers draw a line from the edge of the crater to one of three scorched pits, and a ring blooms on the pit he has chosen. The answer: off the line and out of the ring. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "My host arrived by air, as a roast should: a trail of embers, a plate set at one of three pits. I stepped aside for the dish and kept off the plate. Served hot.",
      oathbroker: "The Dragonfall is a summons served in the air, with the place of delivery named only as he commits: one of three pits. The fine print is the line he flies along. Clear of both. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "He came from the sky along a line of fire. I watched for the ring where he would land. Then I stepped aside, to one side of the line. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Dive. Ember line from the rim to one of three pits. The ring shows which. Moved out sideways, away from both. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "The mark flew, and I loved it. A line of embers across the floor and a ring where it would land. I waited out of both and slipped back in the moment it touched down. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "He flew right over my head and I gasped! The embers drew a line and then a ring blossomed, the colour of trouble, at one of three pits. I stepped out of both. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Dive: hot line, hot ring. Out of both, to the side. Cold read: which pit, then go. I stood in the ring once and burnt. Too far, the other way. Back to the middle.",
      driftblade: "He came down the line of embers and I went across it, through the gap, away from the pit he'd chosen, and out the far side before he landed, and round again, never landing myself.",
      marionettist: "The star made his entrance from the flies, along a line of footlights and onto one of three marks. The company cleared the line and the mark. (A grand entrance. A better exit.)",
      cleric: "The dragon dove, and I watched the line of embers and the ring that bloomed. I told my flock: off the line, and out of the ring. Dawn keep us. We were out, all of us.",
      grovekeeper: "He came like a storm out of a clear sky, along a line of embers. I read where the ring bloomed and moved my lot out of both. Weather you can read is weather you can leave.",
      chronomancer: "The line is drawn well before he comes, and the ring blooms on the pit he picks. I will have stepped off the line on the first beat. I did, for once.",
      alembist: "Ailment: a dive. Symptoms: a line of embers, a ring at the end of it, and three pits to pick from. Remedy: off the line and out of the ring. Label the pits.",
      threadweaver: "He cut across the crater like a pulled thread, and the ring marked where he'd stitch it down. I got every stitch off the line and out of the ring. Mind the slack.",
    } },
    'Twin Pass': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "Two lines of embers at once. He flew the first without landing, then came round on the second and came down. Clear of the first was not enough. Held the ground, and moved twice.",
      gloomsworn: "Two roads of ember. The first he only flew over; the second he landed on. I left one, then the other, and did not rest between. Rest comes later. I have been promised it.",
      thresher: "Two roads of embers. He only flies over the first and comes down on the second, so I stepped off one, then off the other, and didn't sit down between. Not the plot I'd have chosen to lie in.",
      bloodreaver: "Two lines! The first he only passes over; the second ends in a ring and a landing. I moved clear of the first, then clear of the second. A cheat, I call that, and I loved it.",
      runeguard: "The omen: two lines drawn, the later one fainter. The answer: the first is only a pass, the second ends in a landing, and both must be left. Not foreseen; now it is.",
      gorgemaw: "My host serves two courses from the air: the first only flies over the table, the second lands on it. I stepped clear of both, in order. The second was the better.",
      oathbroker: "Two writs, served in sequence. The first is a flyover with no landing; the second carries the ring. The fine print is that the second is drawn while the first is still being served. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "He spoke twice, along two lines. The first passed over; the second landed. I watched the first, then the second. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Two lines. First he only passes. Second he lands. Out of the first, then out of the second. Do not stop after the first. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "The mark made two passes, and I admired the planning. The second line is the one that ends in a landing. I moved clear of both, in turn. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "Twice! He did it twice! A line for the pass and another for the landing, and the second one is the one that bites. I got out of the first only to find the second. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Two passes: first only over, second down. Cold: step clear of the first, read the second, step again. I stopped after the first once. Too far, the wrong way. Back to the middle.",
      driftblade: "Two lines and I ran across the first, through it, and over to the clear patch, and through the second just before it lit, and round, and never landed, and it was glorious.",
      marionettist: "A double entrance: the star crosses the stage once without stopping, and then returns to land on his mark. The company must clear both. (Quick exits, all round.)",
      cleric: "Two lines in the sky. The first he only flew over; the second he landed on. I told my flock: clear of the first, then clear of the second. Dawn keep us, we were.",
      grovekeeper: "Two gusts, one after the other, and the second one is the one that lands. Everybody stepped off the first line, then off the second. Plant first, and move twice.",
      chronomancer: "Two lines on two beats, and the second lands a beat after the first has gone over. I will have stepped off the first and then the second. This time I did.",
      alembist: "Ailment: a double dive. Symptoms: the first line is only a pass; the second ends in a landing. Remedy: clear of both, in that order. Label both lines.",
      threadweaver: "Two long threads across the crater, the first only passing through, the second tying down at a pit. My stitches stepped clear of one and then the other. Mind the slack.",
    } },
    'The Roost': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "He perched on the rim and shook his burning scales loose onto the floor, three at a time. Two whelps came down with them. The line kept moving off the scales and put the whelps down. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "He perched high and shed fiery scales in threes, two whelps dropping with them. We never stopped moving off the scales, and the whelps were dead before he came down. Idle hands are for graves.",
      thresher: "He sat up on the rim and shook his burning scales loose, always one patch under somebody, so I kept walking. Two little whelps came down with them, and I put them in the ground before he dropped. Not ripe, but due.",
      bloodreaver: "The big one sat on the rim and rained burning scales on us, and two little ones came to bite. Good fun. Keep moving, kill the little ones before he drops, or they go off.",
      runeguard: "The omen: he perches high and the scales fall, three at a time, always one under one of us. The answer: keep moving, put the whelps down before he comes to the ground, or they burst. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "My host sat on the rim and shook his burning crumbs onto the floor, and sent two small portions to nibble at us. Better to eat the portions than let them cool and burst. Crunchy.",
      oathbroker: "The Roost is a long recess with penalties: scales fall on named tiles, one under each party in turn, and two small bailiffs come to collect. The fine print is that they burst if they outlive the recess. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "He sat on the rim, high. Fire fell in threes. Two small ones came at us. I stepped aside each time, and broke the small ones before he came down. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Perched on the rim. Scales fall in threes, one under someone. Two whelps. Kept moving, shot the whelps down before he drops. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "The mark perched on the rim and wept fire, three tiles at a time, and one was always under somebody. The whelps were rude. I put them down before he came to the ground. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "He sat on the rim and flaked fire onto the floor like a bonfire shedding sparks, and I loved it, and kept moving! The two little dragons must be put down before he lands. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Scales fall hot, in threes. Step out. Whelps bite: put them down. Cold read: they burst if left. I left one once. Back to the middle, with an empty sleeve.",
      driftblade: "He sat on the rim and burning scales fell in threes and I ran between them, round them, through the gaps, and killed the little dragons on the way past, never landing once.",
      marionettist: "The star took the balcony and showered the stalls with fire, three at a time, one on someone each time. Two small understudies came on. The company must dismiss them before he descends.",
      cleric: "The old dragon sat on the rim and let fire rain on us, always one patch on one of my flock. The whelps harried them. I told them: keep moving, put the little ones down. Dawn keep us.",
      grovekeeper: "It rained fire from the rim, three patches at a time, and I had my lot keep moving through it like walking in a hailstorm. The whelps are saplings of fire: pull them before he lands.",
      chronomancer: "The scales fall a beat after he shakes. Three at a time, always one under somebody. I will have moved on the first beat. The whelps burst at the end if they are still there. I'd put them down early.",
      alembist: "Ailment: the Roost. Symptoms: burning scales in threes, two whelps, a recess of some length. Remedy: keep moving, put the whelps down before he lands, or they burst. Shelve with the scorch kit.",
      threadweaver: "The scales fell like loose pins, three at a time, always one over one of my stitches. Keep moving, keep the whelps down. They burst if they are still there when he comes to the ground.",
    } },
    'Crater Boils': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The ring of floor by the rim began to glow, and it stayed that way. From then on, we fought on the inner ground only. I kept the line in from the edge for the rest of the night. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "The edge of the floor began to glow and never stopped. We were given less room after that, so I kept us to the middle for the rest of the night. I have fought in smaller places.",
      thresher: "The rim went from ember to flame and never cooled, so the field is smaller for the rest of the night. I kept to the inner ground, away from the edge, like ploughing short of a ditch.",
      bloodreaver: "The rim boiled, and it stays boiled. A smaller room to hit him in. I like it close. Keep in from the edge, the glow bites for good.",
      runeguard: "The omen: the rim brightens and the stone along it weeps. The answer: it does not cool, so the room is smaller for the rest of the fight. Keep from the edge. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "My host set the rim to boil, and it does not stop. The table shrank for the rest of the meal, and the edges are too hot to touch. I sat nearer the middle. Reduced, and rich.",
      oathbroker: "The Boil is a permanent amendment: the ring of floor by the rim is forfeit for the remainder. The fine print is that it does not cool. We keep from the edge. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "The rim boiled. It did not stop. The room was smaller after. I stayed inside, away from the edge. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Rim boils. Stays boiled. Smaller room. Kept inside the glow, away from the edge. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "The mark cooked the rim. Nowhere to hide on the edge now, which was my favourite place. Kept to the inner floor, where he looks. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "The whole rim lit up like the best bonfire I have ever seen, and it stays lit! The room is smaller, and my favourite corners are lava. I stand in the middle now. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Rim goes hot, stays hot. Smaller floor. Cold: keep to the middle, off the edge. I stepped on it once and swung. Back to the middle, the whole night.",
      driftblade: "The rim lit up, all the way round, and stayed lit, and I could not run the wall any more, which offends me, so I ran circles in the middle instead, through everything.",
      marionettist: "The edges of the stage caught fire and stayed so. The company was confined to the middle for the rest of the act. (The Doll, being small, did not mind.)",
      cleric: "The rim began to burn and did not stop. I told my flock to keep from the edge, and to mind where they stepped when they ran. Dawn keep us on the inner ground.",
      grovekeeper: "The edge of the crater went from ember to flame, and it does not come back. Plant nothing there. My lot keep to the middle now, where the ground still takes root.",
      chronomancer: "The rim glows a beat after he stamps, and from then on it will have always been glowing. We stayed in from the edge. The room was smaller, and so was the margin.",
      alembist: "Ailment: the Boil. Symptoms: the ring of floor by the rim burns for good. Remedy: stay in from the edge. Shelve nothing near it.",
      threadweaver: "The edge unpicked itself into fire, and no thread will hold there. Keep every stitch in from the rim. A smaller hem, but a cleaner one.",
    } },
    'Twin Breath': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "Two fans of fire at two of us, the second a heartbeat after the first. The line watched the first go, and did not step into the second. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "Two breaths, two of us, the second a moment behind. We left the first and looked before stepping, because the second was waiting there. Dying twice in a row is not on my list.",
      thresher: "Two breaths at two of us, the second a beat behind the first. I stepped out of the first and looked before I stepped again, because the second was waiting right where I meant to go. Two weathers in one afternoon.",
      bloodreaver: "Two cones, two targets, one behind the other! The trick is not to leap out of the first right into the second. I stayed with the big one and let them dance.",
      runeguard: "The omen: two heads of the same breath, the second a beat behind. The answer: leave the first, and look before you step, for the second may be waiting. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "Two flambes, one after the other, at two different guests. Step out of yours and look before stepping into the next. I did not eat either one. Over-cooked.",
      oathbroker: "The fine print of the Twin Breath: a second writ follows the first by a beat. Those who escaped the first were served the second. Clear of both. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "He spoke twice in fire. The first, then the second. I did not run from the first into the second. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Two cones, two of us, one after the other. Step out sideways from the first, then check the second. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "The mark breathed twice, at two others, and I admired the timing. Do not leap out of the first into the second. I stood at its flank and watched. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "Two breaths, and not at me! Rude. The second one is a beat behind the first, so when I was marked I stepped sideways and then looked before I moved again. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Breath, then breath. Step aside from the first, look, then step. I went from one into the other once and ran hot. Back to the middle.",
      driftblade: "Two fans of fire, one behind the other, and I ran across the first and through the gap and out the side of the second, round them both and never landing, and almost didn't see it.",
      marionettist: "The star breathed twice, at two different members of the company, a beat apart. Leave the first spotlight and check the second before stepping. (The Doll was in the wings, as ever.)",
      cleric: "Two fires, one after the other, at two of my flock. I told them: step aside from the first, and look before you step again. Dawn keep them. One of them forgot.",
      grovekeeper: "The first gust of fire, and a second right behind it. My lot stepped out of the first and into nothing, if they looked. Plant first, and look both ways.",
      chronomancer: "The second breath lands a beat after the first. I will have stepped out of the first on its beat, and stayed out of the second on its beat. The second was the hard one.",
      alembist: "Ailment: two breaths, a beat apart, at two targets. Remedy: leave the first sideways, check the second, then move again. Label both flasks.",
      threadweaver: "Two fans of fire, one behind the other. Step out sideways from mine, and check the second seam before pulling anyone through. Mind the slack.",
    } },
    'Heart Burn': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The Heart opened and he could not be hurt. Scorch marks bloomed at the three pits one after another, and the last one marked where the fire would not reach. The line stood round it, off the mark. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "The Heart opened and nothing could touch him. Three scorches came up in turn; the last is where the great fire does not fall. We gathered round it, never on it. The first two taught me which.",
      thresher: "His heart opened and nothing of ours would bite. Scorches came up at the pits one after another, and the last one is the only ground the great fire spares. I stood close round it, off the scorch, and waited for it to come in.",
      bloodreaver: "His heart opened in his chest, and I could not touch him. Three marks, one after another, and the last is where the fire does not go. I stood by it, and not on it, and bled for nothing at all.",
      runeguard: "The omen: three marks bloom in turn, and the third is where the great fire will not fall. The answer: when the first two are known, the third is known; stand around it, but not on it. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "My host opened his heart, and we were not to touch. Three little dishes were set out in turn, and the last was the only seat the fire did not reach. We sat round it. Not on it. Rich.",
      oathbroker: "The Heart is a stay of proceedings: no claim may be made against him. The fine print is the order of the three marks: the last is the island, and it is the only ground that is not forfeit. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "His heart opened. I could not strike. Three marks came in turn; the last is the quiet place. Stand beside it, not on it. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Heart open, untouchable. Three scorches in order. The last one is where the fire stops. Stood around it, not on it. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "The mark opened its heart, which was almost indecent. Three scorches, and the last is the only quiet ground. We stood round it, not on it. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "His heart opened and I could not burn it, which was an insult! Three scorches bloomed, and the last was the quiet place in the fire. I stood round it, not on it. Mostly unsinged, just.",
      thermist: "Heart open, nothing to hit. Three marks, in turn. The last is the cold place. Stand round it, not on it. I stood on it once and ran hot. Back to the middle. Not that middle.",
      driftblade: "His heart was open and I could not cut it, so I ran. Three scorches bloomed one after another, and the last was the quiet place, and I was there before the fire and round the mark.",
      marionettist: "Act the last. The star opens his heart and all the footlights go out but three, and the last of them is the only light that stays lit. The company must stand round it, not in it.",
      cleric: "His heart opened, and no blow of ours could touch him. Three marks, and the last was the quiet place in the fire. I called my flock round it, not on it. Dawn keep us. We were all there.",
      grovekeeper: "A fire comes over everything but the one place. Three marks, in turn, and the last is the clear ground. My lot stand round it, not on it. Plant first, and know where the last is.",
      chronomancer: "Three marks, three beats, and the last is where the fire does not fall. I knew from the second mark which it would be. I will have stood there before it bloomed. I did.",
      alembist: "Ailment: the Heart Burn. Symptoms: a floor-wide fire, three marks in turn, one island. Remedy: the last mark is the island; stand round it, not on it. Label the third flask.",
      threadweaver: "The fire came over the whole floor but one hole in it. Three marks, and the last is the hole. I drew every stitch to it, round the mark and not on it. Mind the slack.",
    } },
    'Wingbeat': { hard: true, learned: {
      bastion: "His wings beat as he flew, and everything near the line was shoved away from it. I stood far enough from the line that it only nudged me, and held my footing. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "The wingbeat threw everything near his flight line outward. I stood well back from it and felt only a nudge. Nearer, you meet the wall; I keep a good distance from both.",
      thresher: "His wings stirred a gale down the dive road, and anyone near it was tossed like chaff off the threshing floor. I stood well back from the road, not just off it, and kept clear of the walls besides.",
      bloodreaver: "A shove from his wings, and everyone near the line goes flying! I like a good shove. Stay well back from the line, or be carried away from it, or into the wall.",
      runeguard: "The omen: the wings lift as he enters the line. The answer: those near it are thrown outward, so stand well back from it, or be ready for the wall. Not foreseen; now it is.",
      gorgemaw: "My host's wings carried a gust that threw the diners from the table's middle. I took my plate to the far end, well away from the line, and stayed seated. Blown, not eaten.",
      oathbroker: "The Wingbeat is a rider to the dive: all parties near the line are removed from it by force. The fine print is where they are removed to. Stand well back, or choose the landing. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "His wings spoke, and everything near the line was pushed away. I stood far from it, and was not pushed. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Wingbeat. Everyone near the line is thrown clear of it. Stood off, well back, no push. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "His wings threw everyone near the line aside, which was rude of him. I was already far from it, naturally. It never saw me, and neither did the wall.",
      pyromancer: "He flapped, and the gust threw my hair back and my friends across the floor! Stay well back from the line, or be thrown into the wall. Mostly unsinged, and a little windswept.",
      thermist: "Wingbeat: cold air, everyone near the line thrown out. Stay far from it, not just clear of it. I stood close once, and swung, and hit the wall. Back to the middle.",
      driftblade: "His wings threw a gust across the line and I rode it, out along the push and through the gap at the end, round and away, never landing, and not into the wall.",
      marionettist: "The star's wings fanned the stage and threw the company to the wings. Stand well back from his entrance, or be carried off. (My Doll was blown into the orchestra. Unhurt.)",
      cleric: "His wings threw my flock away from the line, and one met the wall and cried out. Dawn keep her. I told them: stand well back, not merely clear, and I mended what I could.",
      grovekeeper: "The wings stirred a gale along the line and everyone near it was blown away like leaves. Stand well back, and the gale only ruffles. Keep from the edge, too.",
      chronomancer: "The gust comes a beat before the dive itself, and everyone near the line is thrown. I stood far back on that beat. Last time, which was next time, I stood closer, and learned.",
      alembist: "Ailment: the Wingbeat, a gust along the line that throws everyone near it. Remedy: stand well back, or accept the wall. Note: the wall is not a cure.",
      threadweaver: "His wings pulled every thread near the line out sideways, and one stitch hit the wall. Stand well back from the line, and keep clear of the edge. Mind the slack.",
    } },
    'Cinder Rain': { hard: true, learned: {
      bastion: "Embers fell across the crater, each in a little circle that burned afterwards. I held my ground and watched for the circles, and moved only when one landed near me. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "Embers fell everywhere in small circles, each leaving a burning patch. I walked clear of whichever came near me and no further. There was no hurry in it.",
      thresher: "Embers dropped in little circles all over the crater, each leaving a burning pool. I kept moving, watched where the next would come up, and went round. Plenty of fresh holes out there to fall into; I took none.",
      bloodreaver: "Sparks! All over the floor, and each leaves a pool. A scar for every one, if you like, and I do not, today. Keep moving, and watch the little circles.",
      runeguard: "The omen: small circles bloom one after another across the whole crater. The answer: each leaves a pool, so watch where the next one appears, and do not stand still. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "A shower of sparks from the great oven. Little circles of heat, each leaving a puddle of sauce. I ate none, and moved along the table. Over-seasoned.",
      oathbroker: "The Rain is a series of small claims, each against a named tile, each leaving a lien on the ground. The fine print is that they come one after another. Clear each in turn. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "Embers fell, one at a time, all over. Each left a small fire. I stepped aside from each in turn. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Cinder rain. Small circles, one after another, all over the floor. Each leaves a pool. Kept moving, kept clear. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "Sparks fell all over the crater, and each left a pool. A fine thing to watch, from the shadows. I kept moving, between the circles. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "It RAINED fire! Little circles blooming all over the floor, each one leaving a puddle of lava! I have never been so happy or so busy. Mostly unsinged, if you ignore the hem.",
      thermist: "Embers, hot, small, many. Step aside from each and off the pools. I ran hot with joy and stepped in one. Back to the middle. Carefully.",
      driftblade: "The embers fell all over the crater and I ran between them, through the gaps, round the pools, never landing, never stopping, and the floor behind me burned in my footsteps.",
      marionettist: "A shower of sparks from the flies, each landing in a small bright circle, and each leaving a hot patch on the boards. The company kept to the dark. (The Doll adored it.)",
      cleric: "Embers fell in little circles all over the floor, and every one left a pool. I told my flock: keep moving, watch for the next. Dawn keep us. Nobody stood still.",
      grovekeeper: "The embers came like seeds scattered by a careless hand, and where each fell, a pool of fire. Keep moving, step round them, and plant nothing there. My lot did.",
      chronomancer: "Each ember lands a beat after the one before it. I will have stepped aside from the first, and the next, and the next. I kept the rhythm, mostly.",
      alembist: "Ailment: Cinder Rain. Symptoms: many small circles, each leaving a pool. Remedy: keep moving, step clear of each in turn. Do not shelve anything on the floor.",
      threadweaver: "Embers fell like pins across the whole floor, each a small hole in the cloth. Step clear of each, and off the pools they leave. Mind the slack.",
    } },
    'Heart Flare': { hard: true, learned: {
      bastion: "The Heart flared. One of us was marked for a hit we had to share, and I closed the line on them; and the moment it landed we scattered, each to our own patch. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "A ring over one of us to be shared, so we closed in on it. The instant it landed there were rings over everyone, and we went apart, each to a space of our own. First gather, then leave.",
      thresher: "First a ring over one of us to share, so we all stood in close like sheaves in a stook. The moment it came in, a ring over each head, so out to our own ground. Together, then apart, one season after the other.",
      bloodreaver: "A flare! First everyone piles onto the one who is marked, then we all fly apart before the second blow. A fine scar, and a good dance.",
      runeguard: "The omen: a ring over one of us, to be shared; and the instant it lands, marks over all. The answer: together first, then apart. Not foreseen; now it is.",
      gorgemaw: "A course for the table, then dessert for each. First all sit down together at the marked seat and share it, then each rises and takes a plate of their own. Rich.",
      oathbroker: "The Flare is a two-part instrument: a shared debt, then individual claims. The fine print is the order. Stand together, then stand alone. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "He spoke once, to all of us in the ring. Then he spoke to each of us alone. We stood together first, then apart. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Ring on one of us, share it. Then marks on everyone. Together, then apart. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "The mark flared, and I stood in the ring with the rest, which I hate, and then I went to my own corner as fast as I could, which I love. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "A shared flare, and then marks over everyone's head! Together first, then apart, as fast as possible. I forgot the second part once. Mostly unsinged, just barely.",
      thermist: "Ring: shared, hot. Everyone in. Then marks: out, apart, each alone. I swung between the two and ran hot, then cold. Back to the middle. Then out.",
      driftblade: "The ring came and I hated standing in it with everyone, then the marks came and I ran out of the ring and across the floor and through the others' patches, to my own, never landing.",
      marionettist: "Curtain call in two parts: the whole company bows together, and the moment it ends, each steps downstage alone. (The Doll was always alone. It's a gift.)",
      cleric: "He flared. First we stood together in the ring, and the hit was shared; then marks fell on each of us, and we scattered. Dawn keep us. I mended the ones who forgot the second half.",
      grovekeeper: "First the weather gathers us in, and the flare breaks over the lot; then it breaks again over each alone. Together, then scatter. Plant first, and know which half is next.",
      chronomancer: "The second part lands a beat after the first, and I will have moved on that beat. The first is shared, the second is not. I stood in the ring a beat too long once.",
      alembist: "Ailment: Heart Flare. Symptoms: a shared dose, then a separate one for each. Remedy: together first, then apart. Keep the flasks in two groups.",
      threadweaver: "The first was shared, so I drew every thread in tight; the second was for each, so I cut them loose the instant the first landed. A neat piece of cutting. Mind the slack.",
    } },
  },
};
